{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1446626-anyone-else-dissapointed-with-article-4","id":1446626,"title":"Anyone else dissapointed with Article 4?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-30T10:21:24-07:00","id":1446626,"title":"Anyone else dissapointed with Article 4?","content":"So, I downloaded my Backer copy of Technocracy Reloaded today, and took a look at the explanations for the Precepts of Damian.<br /> <br /> While the overall tone was grating, the punk cuss like a sailor thing doesn't really feel Technocrat to me, I was actively dismayed by their explanation for Article 4. The explanation they gave is so far off base it somehow managed to convey the exact opposite of what I'd been given to understand was it's meaning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T14:03:15-07:00","id":1446657,"title":"","content":"Crude drill sergeant talk aside, it's basically a shortened version of the explanation of it back in Guide to the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> That's thing with many WoD books, doubly so when it comes to Group/Faction books, much of the fluff is present from an in-universe perspective, as it would likely presented to the PCs. Usually this takes the form of in-universe text (whether articles, letters, reports or clips from books) or in the case of this chapter, spoken by a person. In this case, the whole chapter is basically a training briefing for young Technocracts in the style of a drill sergeant, likely a way it would be presented to Technocrats that serve on the frontlines rather than work in the labs which is how GotT handled it's version of the explanation. Which also makes sense as the chapter it's in, Targets, Assets, Tactics and Plans, is all about the matters pertaining to the Union's frontline activities.<br /> <br /> Not everyone in the Technocracy is a stuffy bureaucrat, a geeky labrat or an emotionless operative. Despite what they like to say and present themselves as, the Union is not a monolith.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T14:36:43-07:00","id":1446660,"title":"","content":"Other than the language used, I have no problem with it, at all. It fits my own preference of how Enlightened Science differs from Magick, to a tee: Arete is about Enlightened <i>Will</i> (thus, \u201cWillworking\u201d), whereas Enlightenment is about <i>Enlightened</i> Will (thus my house-rule that Enlightenment is <i>not</i> capped by Willpower, but that those with Enlightenment can never Work Without Focus or surpass their Instruments). Knowing what <i>is</i> is more important than willing what you <i>want</i> to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T15:27:27-07:00","id":1446669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1446626-anyone-else-dissapointed-with-article-4?p=1446657#post1446657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crude drill sergeant talk aside, it's basically a shortened version of the explanation of it back in Guide to the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> That's thing with many WoD books, doubly so when it comes to Group/Faction books, much of the fluff is present from an in-universe perspective, as it would likely presented to the PCs. Usually this takes the form of in-universe text (whether articles, letters, reports or clips from books) or in the case of this chapter, spoken by a person. In this case, the whole chapter is basically a training briefing for young Technocracts in the style of a drill sergeant, likely a way it would be presented to Technocrats that serve on the frontlines rather than work in the labs which is how GotT handled it's version of the explanation. Which also makes sense as the chapter it's in, Targets, Assets, Tactics and Plans, is all about the matters pertaining to the Union's frontline activities.<br /> <br /> Not everyone in the Technocracy is a stuffy bureaucrat, a geeky labrat or an emotionless operative. Despite what they like to say and present themselves as, the Union is not a monolith.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's more or less what I figured they were going for, but I personally didn't really see it as... working. It felt like they tried way too hard.<br /> <br /> In any case my main issue is not with the presentation so much as it is the actual way it's presented. Because it is the exact opposite of the shortened explanation of it back in Guide to the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> To quote the Guide to the Technocracy &quot;If these models can't be fixed to represent the real world, then the world must be altered to fit the Technocracy's Abstractions.&quot; In Guide to the Technocracy it is very much about defining what the world is and destroying anything that goes outside that abstract ideal of how the world 'should be' There's even discussion of incidents like what happened to the Etherites, where the world was defined in a certain way not because it represented some until recently undiscovered truth, but because it would settle a political issue within the union itself.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile the 'slut for learning' approach taken in Technocracy reloaded not only doesn't fit this previous interpretation, it doesn't even fit the article itself. &quot;The Elemental Forces of the Universe cannot be left to the Caprices of the Unknown.&quot; It's a command to be, in essence, know how everything works. A command that not only does the SFL approach not fulfil, but the SFL approach actively defies by surrendering all initiative to the idea that you don't know everything, and that you shouldn't want to anyway because learning new things is amazing.<br /> <br /> Like the very idea of a 'Reality Deviant' does not make sense within this framework of Article 4, as you're not defining reality in the sense of building a framework and demanding reality adhere to it, and destroying anything that deviates from that abstract vision/framework.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T15:58:38-07:00","id":1446677,"title":"","content":"You\u2019re talking about comparing the pre and post Avatar Storm Technocracy. The fact that the former had become come corruptly totalitarian, while the latter thanks to the cutting off of Control, has the opportunity to seize the Daedalen principles they claim to believe in, like actual science and discovery, is a major theme in the line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T16:09:28-07:00","id":1446679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1446626-anyone-else-dissapointed-with-article-4?p=1446677#post1446677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You\u2019re talking about comparing the pre and post Avatar Storm Technocracy. The fact that the former had become come corruptly totalitarian, while the latter thanks to the cutting off of Control, has the opportunity to seize the Daedalen principles they claim to believe in, like actual science and discovery, is a major theme in the line.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The issue is even with that, it's still a sharp divide from the post-avatar storm Technocracy. Because 'Actual Science and Discovery' have <b>never</b> been the Technocrats MO or principles. They have always been about building a utopia on lies because without the lies there is only madness and chaos, and as long as the masses believe those lies, the lies become truth. This is the primary dividing principle between Etherites and Technocrats.<br /> <br /> Etherites practice actual science of a form we would recognize today. Hypothesis, Experiment, record observations, make conclusions. Technocrats are more philosophers than scientists, and have always used science as a tool rather than an end in and of itself. It's useful insofar as they can put their thumb on the scale without anyone noticing. They build ideal models of the world, build out ideal ideas of how it could work and then shoot anyone who defies those models until the consensus settles on those models being true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T16:36:03-07:00","id":1446682,"title":"","content":"The non-diegetic answer is you\u2019re right, but those type of conspiracy theories about mainstream science being a bunch of lies are a lot less cute in 2021 than they were in the 90s, and they don\u2019t want to publish a game for anti-vaxx QAnon following climate change deniers.<br /> <br /> (I\u2019m not calling you that, I\u2019m say that is why a lot of people have grown really uncomfortable with the older role of the Union in the setting. Things that were funny X-Files plotlines in the 90s are now beliefs that have turned loved ones into fascists)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T17:16:54-07:00","id":1446691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1446626-anyone-else-dissapointed-with-article-4?p=1446682#post1446682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The non-diegetic answer is you\u2019re right, but those type of conspiracy theories about mainstream science being a bunch of lies are a lot less cute in 2021 than they were in the 90s, and they don\u2019t want to publish a game for anti-vaxx QAnon following climate change deniers.<br /> <br /> (I\u2019m not calling you that, I\u2019m say that is why a lot of people have grown really uncomfortable with the older role of the Union in the setting. Things that were funny X-Files plotlines in the 90s are now beliefs that have turned loved ones into fascists)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And that at it's core is kind of my issue. They let politics basically dictate that the Union could no longer be the Union, but because of that departure point the whole setting no longer makes sense.<br /> <br /> Because fundementally the world of mage is <i>not </i>our world. In mage, mainstream science <i>is</i> a bunch of lies and you prove it every single time your hermetic hurls a fireball across the street using an Enochian chant. The Etherites prove it every time they break the laws of physics over their knees using disproven science from the dustbin of history. Or a Verbena uses a handful of blood covered leaves to prevent you from catching the coronavirus for example.<br /> <br /> Like I understand that discomfort, but frankly, if that discomfort is to dictate the setting, the setting is effectively dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T18:17:37-07:00","id":1446707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1446626-anyone-else-dissapointed-with-article-4?p=1446691#post1446691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And that at it's core is kind of my issue. They let politics basically dictate that the Union could no longer be the Union, but because of that departure point the whole setting no longer makes sense.<br /> <br /> Because fundementally the world of mage is <i>not </i>our world. In mage, mainstream science <i>is</i> a bunch of lies and you prove it every single time your hermetic hurls a fireball across the street using an Enochian chant. The Etherites prove it every time they break the laws of physics over their knees using disproven science from the dustbin of history. Or a Verbena uses a handful of blood covered leaves to prevent you from catching the coronavirus for example.<br /> <br /> Like I understand that discomfort, but frankly, if that discomfort is to dictate the setting, the setting is effectively dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the function of fiction is to comment on reality. The origins of Mage are drawn from a specific political and social context of the early to mid 90s that are very different now. There is no such thing as apolitical fiction.<br /> <br /> To leave the setting unchanged defeats the point of printing an edition of a Technocracy book in 2021. We already have a Technocracy book that reflects the social and political context of the 90s. It\u2019s obviously going to reflect the current context in which the writers are writing rather than an anachronistic context.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 04-30-2021, 09:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T18:33:47-07:00","id":1446711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1446626-anyone-else-dissapointed-with-article-4?p=1446707#post1446707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But the function of fiction is to comment on reality. The origins of Mage are drawn from a specific political and social context of the early to mid 90s that are very different now. There is no such thing as apolitical fiction.<br /> <br /> To leave the setting unchanged defeats the point of printing an edition of a Technocracy book in 2021. We already have a Technocracy book that reflects the social and political context of the 90s. It\u2019s obviously going to reflect the current context in which the writers are writing rather than an anachronistic context.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I fundamentally disagree with that notion. Fiction is a means of exploring ideas. Maxwell's Demon is not a political concept, despite being a fictional one. While it certainly allows one to reflect on 'what could be' in more or less real terms, the idea that you could somehow spin Maxwell's Demon into a political stance is a nonsensical one.<br /> <br /> Likewise, the idea that the world of Mage the Ascension, for all that it uses Trappings of our world, could have meaningful political relevance given it shares none of the reality our political structure is based upon is.... well, flawed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T21:59:30-07:00","id":1446740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1446626-anyone-else-dissapointed-with-article-4?p=1446711#post1446711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I fundamentally disagree with that notion. Fiction is a means of exploring ideas. Maxwell's Demon is not a political concept, despite being a fictional one. While it certainly allows one to reflect on 'what could be' in more or less real terms, the idea that you could somehow spin Maxwell's Demon into a political stance is a nonsensical one.<br /> <br /> Likewise, the idea that the world of Mage the Ascension, for all that it uses Trappings of our world, could have meaningful political relevance given it shares none of the reality our political structure is based upon is.... well, flawed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Narrative fiction is different than a thought experiment.<br /> <br /> And you are applying a very narrow definition of \u201cpolitical\u201d if you don\u2019t think what Mage presents with regard to individualism vs communal responsibility, or the consequences of imperialism, etc etc are political. Our relationship to technology and consumerism are political. Politics is not limited to partisan elections.<br /> <br /> The very concept of a \u201cNew World Order\u201d as a black helicopter globalist conspiracy is political. It was a fear dreamed up by nationalists in reaction to the post Cold War international order, an order President George H Bush called the \u201cnew world order\u201d.<br /> <br /> The setting as presented in the 90s was very much based on the social-political zeitgeist of the 90s. Expecting writers in 2021 to write the same things is downright silly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 05-01-2021, 03:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T05:01:10-07:00","id":1446779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1446626-anyone-else-dissapointed-with-article-4?p=1446740#post1446740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The setting as presented in the 90s was very much based on the social-political zeitgeist of the 90s. Expecting writers in 2021 to write the same things is downright silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is silly is to go agaisnt the fundamentals of the fictional setting that one is writing for. In Mage, the qanon antivaxx's point of view is as much valid as those of scientists.<br /> <br /> That may be umpalatable to some, but &quot;commenting on reality&quot; isn't the main goal of an rpg setting. The goal is to make a universe in which you live as a character. <br /> <br /> The cohesion of the setting is more more important than mere political concerns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T10:03:24-07:00","id":1446806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1446626-anyone-else-dissapointed-with-article-4?p=1446779#post1446779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What is silly is to go agaisnt the fundamentals of the fictional setting that one is writing for. In Mage, the qanon antivaxx's point of view is as much valid as those of scientists.<br /> <br /> That may be umpalatable to some, but &quot;commenting on reality&quot; isn't the main goal of an rpg setting. The goal is to make a universe in which you live as a character.<br /> <br /> The cohesion of the setting is more more important than mere political concerns.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m not sure \u201cworld where antisemites are right!\u201d has the appeal to sell a gameline on as a world most players want their characters to live in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T14:04:24-07:00","id":1446846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1446626-anyone-else-dissapointed-with-article-4?p=1446806#post1446806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019m not sure \u201cworld where antisemites are right!\u201d has the appeal to sell a gameline on as a world most players want their characters to live in.</div> </div> </div> </div>It certainly doesn't. But that's not a world Mage actually proposes. There's no indication the consensus affects moral judgements or value judgements any more than it does in the real world. That is to say, if the real world has subjective morality, so does Mage. If the real world has objective morality then, likely, so does Mage.<br /> <br /> It's the anti-vax side that may be right in Mage. That's the physical reality the consensus might actually affect. It's also the element I suspect <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24043\" data-vbnamecard=\"24043\">Nyremne</a> was referring to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T15:37:29-07:00","id":1446855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1446626-anyone-else-dissapointed-with-article-4?p=1446806#post1446806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019m not sure \u201cworld where antisemites are right!\u201d has the appeal to sell a gameline on as a world most players want their characters to live in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Moral values are as subjective in mage as they are in reality.<br /> <br /> We're not talking about values, but concrete events. In mage, if enough people believe it, vaccines will cause autism and drinking urine will effectivelly heal cancer.<br /> <br /> In reality, science is our best method to gather knowledge, in mage, it's merely a set of belief without more demonstrable efficiency than religious faith or mad wisdom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T15:08:53-07:00","id":1447039,"title":"","content":"And this is where I bring up Earthly Foundations, where \u201cif enough people believe it\u201d isn't necessarily the be-all and end-all of what works and what doesn't. That it <i>is</i> a factor is what distinguishes Mage from the real world; but it's only <i>a</i> factor. If there wasn't <i>some</i> sort of clash between \u201chow people believe the world works\u201d and \u201chow the world works\u201d, <i>science</i> wouldn't work. And while we might well still have much of the convenience of modern life, it would more likely take the form of herbal poultices rather than vaccines; flying carpets rather than cars. <br /> <br /> The Earthly Foundations make science and technology possible; without them, progress would be \u201cmore of the same, only better\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T15:30:57-07:00","id":1447046,"title":"","content":"Science doesn't actually works in Mage.<br /> <br /> Modern science is constantly contradicted by the existence of reality zones, or the deep universe, where everything goes.<br /> <br /> And we can see that with historical settings. <br /> <br /> Dark ages mage and sorcerer crusade shows that going out of earth don't lead you to space, victorian mage manuscript mention a possible history where ether science rules the world.<br /> <br /> The only real earthly foundations are not &quot;science works&quot;.<br /> Buy rather -the world exist<br /> -minds exist<br /> -minds with avatar shapes reality<br /> -alternate umbral realms exist and are shaped by previous point, without requiring said minds per se.<br /> -conflicting reality shifting powers are set by the more powerful one, which expel the other.<br /> <br /> Science and tech are literally &quot;more of the same, only better&quot;.<br /> <br /> The first manmade mission to the moon could have been achieved by ethership that spit on any concept of inertia, or by a team of dragon riders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T15:42:25-07:00","id":1447049,"title":"","content":"Once uppon a time, the Technocracy changed from being the guys representing Statism and the Weaver to the &quot;unsung heros of humanity&quot;.<br /> <br /> In a more general note: I agree in that RPG doesn't <i>need </i>to be a commentary on reality (albeit some commentary could be inevitable) - but I also want to very much break a lance in favor of the rigth of authors to heavily comment on reality, if they want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T17:45:38-07:00","id":1447062,"title":"","content":"They can comment on reality, but not at the cost of the axioms of the setting they are writing on","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T19:33:28-07:00","id":1447087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1446626-anyone-else-dissapointed-with-article-4?p=1446779#post1446779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What is silly is to go agaisnt the fundamentals of the fictional setting that one is writing for. In Mage, the qanon antivaxx's point of view is as much valid as those of scientists.<br /> <br /> That may be umpalatable to some, but &quot;commenting on reality&quot; isn't the main goal of an rpg setting. The goal is to make a universe in which you live as a character.<br /> <br /> The cohesion of the setting is more more important than mere political concerns.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except it is with WoD. Commenting on real world socio-politics has always been a part of the setting.<br /> <br /> From the framing of Camarilla vs Anarchs (and the framing of Clan Brujah as rabble-rousing rebels), the entirety of Werewolf being about climate change and playing as eco-terrorists (and even the Black Furies being portrayed as militant feminists or the Pure Tribes as Native American werewolves), and Wraith having a whole goddamn sourcebook devoted to talking about the Holocaust within the context of Wraith's setting (and to this day is praised as being the best WoD to handle a serious topic well and sensitively).<br /> <br /> It's one thing to say if you personally don't play out the WoD like that in your games. But it's completely false and misleading to say WoD was never like this at all in the official text.<br /> <br /> This isn't like D&amp;D where intentional socio-politics are subtextual at best. WoD it was ALWAYS textual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T20:36:53-07:00","id":1447094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1446626-anyone-else-dissapointed-with-article-4?p=1447046#post1447046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Science doesn't actually works in Mage.<br /> <br /> Modern science is constantly contradicted by the existence of reality zones, or the deep universe, where everything goes.<br /> <br /> And we can see that with historical settings.<br /> <br /> Dark ages mage and sorcerer crusade shows that going out of earth don't lead you to space, victorian mage manuscript mention a possible history where ether science rules the world.<br /> <br /> The only real earthly foundations are not &quot;science works&quot;.<br /> Buy rather -the world exist<br /> -minds exist<br /> -minds with avatar shapes reality<br /> -alternate umbral realms exist and are shaped by previous point, without requiring said minds per se.<br /> -conflicting reality shifting powers are set by the more powerful one, which expel the other.<br /> <br /> Science and tech are literally &quot;more of the same, only better&quot;.<br /> <br /> The first manmade mission to the moon could have been achieved by ethership that spit on any concept of inertia, or by a team of dragon riders.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Magic works&quot; doesn't mean &quot;science doesn't work.&quot;<br /> <br /> Science is a methodology for forming knowledge about the external world. Technology then builds on that knowledge of the world. You are right that &quot;modern science,&quot; whether you mean &quot;science in Reality&quot; or &quot;non-Enlightened science in the World of Darkness,&quot; is contradicted by Reality Zones, the Deep Umbra, etc. But adding new aspects to reality, new variables to the equation, does not necessarily invalidate that methodology, especially since that methodology is distinct from the alternative, magic, in significant ways.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T21:36:34-07:00","id":1447102,"title":"","content":"One of the things is that in Mage, holistic medicine and such actually work, or at least they can work if the right individual is administering the medicine, or if it's being used in the right place. Anti-vaxx can also work. In the real world if a child has cancer and his parents call in a faith healer to pray for him instead of taking him to chemotherapy, those parents can (and should) be arrested. In the World of Darkness though, faith healers can cure blindness and cancer through prayer, so it could be viewed as entirely reasonable if the family brings in a member of the Celestial Chorus or Dreamspeakers who can do something like that. And, of course, the Technocracy would respond by trying to hunt down and imprison or kill the &quot;reality deviant&quot; who gives families an option of how to treat their child's cancer. <br /> <br /> MtA isn't necessarily &quot;anti-science&quot; but to a degree, modern science, medicine, etc are largely the tools of the Technocracy, a vast conspiracy puppetteering the world from the shadows. Many of the Traditions are pushing for a world in which the sorts of things that don't work in <i>our</i>, real life world, will be able to work on a large scale in the World of Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T22:49:09-07:00","id":1447116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1446626-anyone-else-dissapointed-with-article-4?p=1447046#post1447046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Science doesn't actually works in Mage.<br /> <br /> Modern science is constantly contradicted by the existence of reality zones, or the deep universe, where everything goes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Science works very well in Mage, because science is a type of codified magic with an efficacy built upon reinforcement by an indoctrinated Consensus. Other forms of magic are likewise codified, through theory, practice and paradigm, though ultimately they have a degree of flexibility that science does not. It's <i>all </i>magic, and it's all subject to varying degrees of reliability depending on your location. <br /> <br /> As for Article 4, the section initially rubbed me wrong, most particularly because I don't know who the speaker is. I could see this kind of talk from a Syndicate agent, though the content doesn't suggest it. But the style of writing tells the reader that the stereotypical Technocrat may not be the norm, which I like. There's a place for it, though I would have put it in another section.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12765-otto-d-fey","name":"Otto D'Fey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T04:48:25-07:00","id":1447175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1446626-anyone-else-dissapointed-with-article-4?p=1447094#post1447094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Magic works&quot; doesn't mean &quot;science doesn't work.&quot;<br /> <br /> Science is a methodology for forming knowledge about the external world. Technology then builds on that knowledge of the world. You are right that &quot;modern science,&quot; whether you mean &quot;science in Reality&quot; or &quot;non-Enlightened science in the World of Darkness,&quot; is contradicted by Reality Zones, the Deep Umbra, etc. But adding new aspects to reality, new variables to the equation, does not necessarily invalidate that methodology, especially since that methodology is distinct from the alternative, magic, in significant ways.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think it is important to distinguish between the actual methodology of science and the &quot;science&quot; pushed by the Technocracy. The latter is more the appearance (and in some cases an after the fact reproducability) of science without the actual methodology of science. The methodology of science, though not impossible in Mage, is very difficult and not something most Technocrats or anyone else really practices.<br /> <br /> Now it is arguable that the Technocracy's methodical approach to embedding principles in the consensus is a reasonable approach to scientific endeavor in a world of subjective reality. That doesn't separate it from more magical methodologies, though. As @Otto_D'Fey says, it's a type of codified magic.<br /> <br /> Now I don't think that the Technocracy's approach to science is irreconcilable with the in character speech about Article 4. Indeed, as a pep talk it reads very much like someone who understands that perceptions (both Sleeper and Technocrat) affect the results but who also doesn't want that specific perception at the forefront of anyone's mind.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 05-03-2021, 07:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T06:55:07-07:00","id":1447186,"title":"","content":"I think it's also important to consider the notion of <i>unintended consequences</i>: you get two very different impressions of the Union depending on whether every aspect of their technology was deliberately chosen, or not. If everything is deliberate, then the Technocrats are a bunch of sadists who deliberately choose to promote technologies that cause cancer, lung disease, environmental destruction, and all other manners of pain and devastation; of not, then they're arrogant idealists who are too full of themselves to properly consider the consequences of their actions. Former strikes me more as Nephandi territory; and in fact Book of the Fallen has a number of types of Nephandi which could loosely be described as \u201c[insert Convention here], but sadistic\u201d. As such, I tend to prefer the well intentioned extremist take on the Technocracy. <br /> <br /> Some of this can be chalked up to the Paradox Effect, or some variant thereof; but some of it can't. There are some choices that the Technocracy has made in developing their technology that simply don't make sense if everything was driven by belief or willworking. Which is where my citation of Earthly Foundations comes in: these ground rules, which exist even when a given Reality Zone has been completely depopulated (see the Kickstarter manuscript for Victorian Mage) and include such things as \u201cwater flowing uphill is always Vulgar\u201d, provide an objective element to the setting that Traditionists tend to ignore, but (in my view of them) the Technocracy embraces. At the very least, a Technocrat can justify the Union's design choices as \u201cthat's what's most compatible with the Earthly Foundations\u201d. <br /> <br /> It also gives Enlightened Scientists something to apply the scientific method to: they're students of the Earthly Foundations. And that's where Technocracy Reloaded's take on Article 4 comes in: rather than portray Technocrats as willworkers who are trying to force an arbitrary standard on everyone, it portrays them as Scientists who are trying to force conformity to the Earthly Foundations on everyone, while expressing the fascination that they have with learning everything they can about the Earthly Foundations. That is, it removes the arbitrary nature of their technology. The Technocrats are still control freaks (it is, after all, in their name); but they're <i>also</i> scientists, and not just pretenders. (I have always hated how earlier editions of the game portrayed Technocrats as either liars or dupes: either they know that reality is as the Traditions say it is and are deceiving everyone about it, or they <i>don't</i> know, and are acting out of stupid ignorance. This more nuanced take removes that aspect of things, recasting Enlightened Scientists as people who are focusing on a truth that the <i>Traditions</i> have largely rejected, removing the clear-cut \u201cTraditions are metaphysically right, and Technocrats are metaphysically wrong\u201d distinction. Now, they're both Blind Men groping an Elephant, each focusing on an aspect of the truth but missing something else. You can still critique the Union for trying to force conformity on everyone; but that's distinct from whether or not Enlightened Science has to be a lie. And that, in turn, opens up the possibility of playing an Enlightened Scientist who <i>isn't</i> a Technocrat, and who isn't an \u201canything goes if you just believe\u201d Etherite, either.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T09:10:32-07:00","id":1447210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1446626-anyone-else-dissapointed-with-article-4?p=1447186#post1447186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also gives Enlightened Scientists something to apply the scientific method to: they're students of the Earthly Foundations. And that's where Technocracy Reloaded's take on Article 4 comes in: rather than portray Technocrats as willworkers who are trying to force an arbitrary standard on everyone, it portrays them as Scientists who are trying to force conformity to the Earthly Foundations on everyone, while expressing the fascination that they have with learning everything they can about the Earthly Foundations. That is, it removes the arbitrary nature of their technology. The Technocrats are still control freaks (it is, after all, in their name); but they're <i>also</i> scientists, and not just pretenders. (I have always hated how earlier editions of the game portrayed Technocrats as either liars or dupes: either they know that reality is as the Traditions say it is and are deceiving everyone about it, or they <i>don't</i> know, and are acting out of stupid ignorance. This more nuanced take removes that aspect of things, recasting Enlightened Scientists as people who are focusing on a truth that the <i>Traditions</i> have largely rejected, removing the clear-cut \u201cTraditions are metaphysically right, and Technocrats are metaphysically wrong\u201d distinction. Now, they're both Blind Men groping an Elephant, each focusing on an aspect of the truth but missing something else. You can still critique the Union for trying to force conformity on everyone; but that's distinct from whether or not Enlightened Science has to be a lie. And that, in turn, opens up the possibility of playing an Enlightened Scientist who <i>isn't</i> a Technocrat, and who isn't an \u201canything goes if you just believe\u201d Etherite, either.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I think that a lot of the &quot;either idiots or liars&quot; dilemma goes away when we treat consensual reality as something that's easy to say and hard to understand. From our privileged position we can (if we want to) take a very simple approach, but that is not what it looks like in universe. It took thousands of years for anyone at all to figure out that reality was mutable, and in all that time plenty of people were finding truths, constants, and other important and revelatory things. That didn't stop once the Consensus was &quot;discovered,&quot; nor did everyone give up on the idea of actual truth instantly, or at all. <br /> <br /> There are still truths (seeming truths or otherwise) for the Technocrats to apply their methods to. They aren't liars if those truths aren't the Earthly Foundations, unless you take the approach that everything is a lie.<br /> <br /> Instead, what I think is going on with the Technocracy is that they have to balance three equally important factors:<br /> What will bring about the best results for the world and society? <br /> What can they actually get the sleepers to believe and embrace? <br /> What fits with their own personal and institutional understanding and paradigm? <br /> <br /> This is the element that makes them look more hypocritical and confused than other factions. It's not that they have their head in the sand where others don't, it's that these three factors work against each other and a certain amount of compromise of all three is required. What should be sometimes clashes with what can be and what must be. They are both scientists and aware that they can, with much effort, force the facts to fit the data in a very literal way. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T10:17:46-07:00","id":1447225,"title":"","content":"And you know what? I agree with all of that. It's also fully compatible with everything I just said. In particular, I don't see it as removing the usefulness of having the Earthly Foundations to study. And to my mind, that has an additional benefit of saying that the Traditions don't have all the answers, either. Which, I think, is what so many Mage players bristle about whenever I talk about the Earthly Foundations: it flies in the face of the idea that the Traditions have it all figured out. It's also why they tend to want to downplay the Earthly Foundations to the point where there almost meaningless, as with the earlier claim in this thread that their only value is to describe the rules of Magick. <br /> <br /> As well: the notion that enlightened scientists study the Earthly Foundations is indirectly found in M20. I'm dictating to my phone, so I don't have time right now to look up the exact references; but if you look at the Earthly foundations entry, you'll notice stuff about how blatantly violating physics is always vulgar; and if you look at the technocratic reality Zone section, you'll note a small entry where technocrats claim superiority of their model because it is based on physics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T11:14:55-07:00","id":1447239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1446626-anyone-else-dissapointed-with-article-4?p=1447225#post1447225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And you know what? I agree with all of that. It's also fully compatible with everything I just said. In particular, I don't see it as removing the usefulness of having the Earthly Foundations to study. And to my mind, that has an additional benefit of saying that the Traditions don't have all the answers, either. Which, I think, is what so many Mage players bristle about whenever I talk about the Earthly Foundations: it flies in the face of the idea that the Traditions have it all figured out. It's also why they tend to want to downplay the Earthly Foundations to the point where there almost meaningless, as with the earlier claim in this thread that their only value is to describe the rules of Magick.<br /> <br /> As well: the notion that enlightened scientists study the Earthly Foundations is indirectly found in M20. I'm dictating to my phone, so I don't have time right now to look up the exact references; but if you look at the Earthly foundations entry, you'll notice stuff about how blatantly violating physics is always vulgar; and if you look at the technocratic reality Zone section, you'll note a small entry where technocrats claim superiority of their model because it is based on physics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I very much dislike the idea of the Traditions having all the answers. As far as I am concerned a lot of their party line is a convenient fiction that everyone states but no one fully believes. Ask the nine traditions how magic and consensual reality actually work and you will get 27 different answers, many of them contradictory.<br /> <br /> My reasons for downplaying the Earthly Foundations actually run in the opposite direction. Most of those I've expounded upon at length so I'll try not to do so again, but the important ones in this case are: <br /> <br /> 1) Like you, I don't want either the Traditions or the Technocracy to be more right in any sort of physical or metaphysical sense. Their struggle is largely a moral and philosophical one. Freedom vs safety, individuality vs collective, etc. If one or the other has a privileged position it undercuts that. I'm fine with them claiming such a position, but not with it being true from our point of view.<br /> <br /> 2) I really don't like the idea that the default reality is our reality and all the magic (and hypertech) and wonder are just layered over the top of it. If it's a game of Reality on the Brink it should be all of reality on that brink. <br /> <br /> Now given previous conversations and comments I know you aren't describing either of those. You've been open to the idea of mutable (with great difficulty) Earthly Foundations, which alleviates most of my issues. In my experience that's not what most people mean when they appeal to the EFs though, and so I prefer not to describe the Technocracy as using them.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T08:21:42-07:00","id":1447405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1446626-anyone-else-dissapointed-with-article-4?p=1447186#post1447186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's also important to consider the notion of <i>unintended consequences</i>: you get two very different impressions of the Union depending on whether every aspect of their technology was deliberately chosen, or not. If everything is deliberate, then the Technocrats are a bunch of sadists who deliberately choose to promote technologies that cause cancer, lung disease, environmental destruction, and all other manners of pain and devastation; of not, then they're arrogant idealists who are too full of themselves to properly consider the consequences of their actions. Former strikes me more as Nephandi territory; and in fact Book of the Fallen has a number of types of Nephandi which could loosely be described as \u201c[insert Convention here], but sadistic\u201d. As such, I tend to prefer the well intentioned extremist take on the Technocracy. <br /> <br /> Some of this can be chalked up to the Paradox Effect, or some variant thereof; but some of it can't. There are some choices that the Technocracy has made in developing their technology that simply don't make sense if everything was driven by belief or willworking. Which is where my citation of Earthly Foundations comes in: these ground rules, which exist even when a given Reality Zone has been completely depopulated (see the Kickstarter manuscript for Victorian Mage) and include such things as \u201cwater flowing uphill is always Vulgar\u201d, provide an objective element to the setting that Traditionists tend to ignore, but (in my view of them) the Technocracy embraces. At the very least, a Technocrat can justify the Union's design choices as \u201cthat's what's most compatible with the Earthly Foundations\u201d. <br /> <br /> It also gives Enlightened Scientists something to apply the scientific method to: they're students of the Earthly Foundations. And that's where Technocracy Reloaded's take on Article 4 comes in: rather than portray Technocrats as willworkers who are trying to force an arbitrary standard on everyone, it portrays them as Scientists who are trying to force conformity to the Earthly Foundations on everyone, while expressing the fascination that they have with learning everything they can about the Earthly Foundations. That is, it removes the arbitrary nature of their technology. The Technocrats are still control freaks (it is, after all, in their name); but they're <i>also</i> scientists, and not just pretenders. (I have always hated how earlier editions of the game portrayed Technocrats as either liars or dupes: either they know that reality is as the Traditions say it is and are deceiving everyone about it, or they <i>don't</i> know, and are acting out of stupid ignorance. This more nuanced take removes that aspect of things, recasting Enlightened Scientists as people who are focusing on a truth that the <i>Traditions</i> have largely rejected, removing the clear-cut \u201cTraditions are metaphysically right, and Technocrats are metaphysically wrong\u201d distinction. Now, they're both Blind Men groping an Elephant, each focusing on an aspect of the truth but missing something else. You can still critique the Union for trying to force conformity on everyone; but that's distinct from whether or not Enlightened Science has to be a lie. And that, in turn, opens up the possibility of playing an Enlightened Scientist who <i>isn't</i> a Technocrat, and who isn't an \u201canything goes if you just believe\u201d Etherite, either.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternatively, those issues are where we can see Traditionalist Victories in the Ascension war. Cell phones cause cancer? Of course they don't, says the Technocracy. But a few people showing up with cancer after spending too much time on their phones around a Verbena... Well. People get convinced. Just because the Technocrats caught them out by playing the game first, doesn't mean the traditions can't put their thumbs on the scale of consensus. The most blatant example of which is the Taftani and their sheer vulgarity carving out a reality zone in the middle east.<br /> <br /> And frankly, the Technocrats already violated the Earthly foundations when they created Outer Space from the Umbra and wrote exceptions into Gravity always being pointed towards the ground.<br /> <br /> The earthly foundations are a handwave to justify gravity and ban meaningful time travel and little else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T09:39:03-07:00","id":1447416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1446626-anyone-else-dissapointed-with-article-4?p=1447405#post1447405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Alternatively, those issues are where we can see Traditionalist Victories in the Ascension war. Cell phones cause cancer? Of course they don't, says the Technocracy. But a few people showing up with cancer after spending too much time on their phones around a Verbena... Well. People get convinced. Just because the Technocrats caught them out by playing the game first, doesn't mean the traditions can't put their thumbs on the scale of consensus. The most blatant example of which is the Taftani and their sheer vulgarity carving out a reality zone in the middle east.<br /> <br /> And frankly, the Technocrats already violated the Earthly foundations when they created Outer Space from the Umbra and wrote exceptions into Gravity always being pointed towards the ground.<br /> <br /> The earthly foundations are a handwave to justify gravity and ban meaningful time travel and little else.</div> </div> </div> </div>So: in your setting, the Traditions consider it a win to <i>give people cancer</i>? I must say, that's <i>dark</i>. If that's what they're like, maybe the Union's efforts to eliminate them have some validity\u2026<br /> <br /> Same the Void Engineers didn't <i>create</i> Conventional Space; they <i>discovered</i> it buried under the Umbra. The zero-gravity nature of outer space isn't a violation of the Earthly Foundations (for one thing, they're not that easy to violate); it's <i>part of</i> outer space's Earthly Foundations. <br /> <br /> There's considerably more to the Earthly Foundations than <i>just</i> gravity and (the lack of) meaningful time travel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T10:23:16-07:00","id":1447419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1446626-anyone-else-dissapointed-with-article-4?p=1447416#post1447416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Same the Void Engineers didn't <i>create</i> Conventional Space; they <i>discovered</i> it buried under the Umbra. The zero-gravity nature of outer space isn't a violation of the Earthly Foundations (for one thing, they're not that easy to violate); it's <i>part of</i> outer space's Earthly Foundations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you think that not being able to breathe in Conventional Space is a product of the Earthly Foundations? That seems like something that was not the case, and then later imposed by the Technocratic Paradigm. From what I recall, breathing in space wasn't a problem for Mages until the Technocracy &quot;proved&quot; it was a void without breathable atmosphere. Was it always the case that Mages were altering reality when breathing in space, acting in opposition to the Foundations of that Realm, or did the Technocrats actually impose a new Reality Zone rather than just discovering the Foundations of Conventional Space? Or were Mages just previously never traveling in Conventional Space, but instead in other co-existent Umbral Realms?<br /> <br /> I think some room needs to be left for the Technocracy to still be in the Shaping Reality game. It doesn't even need to take away from the Technocracy trying to discover the truth of the Earthly Foundations. If those Foundations still include some room for multiple outcomes, then the Technocracy can still try to act in accord with the Foundations while also still choosing the option that suits their interests. To bring in my layman's understanding of Tychoidian cosmology, is the Enlightened Anthropic Principle an Earthly Foundation? If it is, or even just close to being one, then you can imagine the Technocracy being able to manipulate conditions in many ways while still acting in accordance with their understanding of the Earthly Foundations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T12:01:59-07:00","id":1447427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1446626-anyone-else-dissapointed-with-article-4?p=1447416#post1447416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So: in your setting, the Traditions consider it a win to <i>give people cancer</i>? I must say, that's <i>dark</i>. If that's what they're like, maybe the Union's efforts to eliminate them have some validity\u2026<br /> <br /> Same the Void Engineers didn't <i>create</i> Conventional Space; they <i>discovered</i> it buried under the Umbra. The zero-gravity nature of outer space isn't a violation of the Earthly Foundations (for one thing, they're not that easy to violate); it's <i>part of</i> outer space's Earthly Foundations. <br /> <br /> There's considerably more to the Earthly Foundations than <i>just</i> gravity and (the lack of) meaningful time travel.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, the idea that coventiona space was discovered and not created qeems to simply be your headcannon. Nothing in any VE book says so and it is contradicted by sorcerer's crusade (daedalians going to space with airships and no breathing gear) and revised VE convention book aboit the expansion of conventional space agaisnt the deep universe","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T12:32:17-07:00","id":1447433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1446626-anyone-else-dissapointed-with-article-4?p=1447416#post1447416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So: in your setting, the Traditions consider it a win to <i>give people cancer</i>? I must say, that's <i>dark</i>. If that's what they're like, maybe the Union's efforts to eliminate them have some validity\u2026<br /> <br /> Same the Void Engineers didn't <i>create</i> Conventional Space; they <i>discovered</i> it buried under the Umbra. The zero-gravity nature of outer space isn't a violation of the Earthly Foundations (for one thing, they're not that easy to violate); it's <i>part of</i> outer space's Earthly Foundations. <br /> <br /> There's considerably more to the Earthly Foundations than <i>just</i> gravity and (the lack of) meaningful time travel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well yes. Just like the Technocracy considers it a win to give people horrific allergies to natural processes in order to combat the back to nature paradigm of the Verbena.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, the Ascension war isn't pretty and the ones who suffer most are the sleepers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T12:52:25-07:00","id":1447434,"title":"","content":"In the same way the technocracy consider it a win when an etherite method to generate free electricity and heal cancer with phlogiston is debunked and rejected by the consensus","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T13:00:12-07:00","id":1447436,"title":"","content":"The Enlightened Anthropic Principle isn't so much an Earthly Foundation as it is their name for what the Traditions call the Metaphysics of Magick: the idea that reality is mutable. But let's go back to Article 1: \u201cbring stasis and order to the universe\u201d. While the phrasing is a holdover from the first edition, the idea that the Union prefers to build and preserve, and tries <i>not</i> to tear down or change, is still very much valid. While there's variance in their ranks (e.g., the Void Engineers have a \u201cResearch and Execution\u201d Department because they can't afford to run their tech development through the same approval process that the other Conventions use; and at the other extreme, the Syndicate takes pride in <i>not</i> having to break out the hypertech), the overall tremendous is toward the conservative. Wild changes such as transforming outer space into a non-breathable environment is not the sort of thing that they'd do without a <i>very</i> good reason, just on principle; add to that the logistical overhead that would be required, and I just don't see them doing it. <br /> <br /> They can engage in the reality shaping game, yes. But they tend to do so by adding to what's already there. And the result of that is that It's usually hard to distinguish their reality shaping from their discoveries. (For what it's worth, I think they easiest way to confirm that something was a discovery rather than reality shaping is to ask whether or not the Technocracy would <i>want</i> a particular outcome: if not, then it's definitely a discovery; of so, it might still be a discovery, or it might be reality shaping. The handful of cases where it's clearly reality shaping are mostly <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/Zeerust\" target=\"_blank\">zeerust</a>: stuff that has been revealed to be reality shaping by a better understanding of the Earthly Foundations that has uncovered a discrepancy. <br /> <br /> So yes, I do believe that not being able to breathe and Conventional Space is a product of the Earthly Foundations. Prior to the mid 20th century, Conventional Space only extended out as far as the moon's orbit. It took a concerted effort by the Void Engineers to push the Spatial Horizon out to the Asteroid Belt, where it is now. In general, even now Mages and Scientists alike tends to travel through Etherspace/Subspace to get where they're going. And there used to be no alternative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T13:22:33-07:00","id":1447439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1446626-anyone-else-dissapointed-with-article-4?p=1447427#post1447427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair, the idea that coventiona space was discovered and not created qeems to simply be your headcannon. Nothing in any VE book says so and it is contradicted by sorcerer's crusade (daedalians going to space with airships and no breathing gear) and revised VE convention book aboit the expansion of conventional space agaisnt the deep universe</div> </div> </div> </div>Back during the Sorcerers Crusade era, the Spatial Horizon was located at the upper edge of the atmosphere. The skyriggers never entered the vacuum of space, because conventional space had not yet expanded out enough for there to be any.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-04-2021, 04:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T13:26:43-07:00","id":1447440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1446626-anyone-else-dissapointed-with-article-4?p=1447433#post1447433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well yes. Just like the Technocracy considers it a win to give people horrific allergies to natural processes in order to combat the back to nature paradigm of the Verbena.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, the Ascension war isn't pretty and the ones who suffer most are the sleepers.</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference is that the Traditions aren't anti-technology. They're just anti-technocracy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T15:08:26-07:00","id":1447457,"title":"","content":"I dislike a confrontalal and casual in-universe lore telling in RPG books. But in universe it\u2019s a single technocrats talking to some noobs. Plus to show the technocracy isn\u2019t a cold and sterile enemy like in 1 dd","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T15:36:51-07:00","id":1447467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1446626-anyone-else-dissapointed-with-article-4?p=1447439#post1447439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back during the Sorcerers Crusade era, the Spatial Horizon was located at the upper edge of the atmosphere. The skyriggers never entered the vacuum of space, because conventional space had not yet expanded out enough for there to be any.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, that's assuming that this vaccuum existed back then.<br /> <br /> Howether, it's pretty contradicted by victorian mage's futures fate.<br /> In one of them, the ether is adopted by the order of reason, which run contrary to the notion of a vacuum.<br /> <br /> I would also add that skyriggers *did* pass the horizon, as they already fought in the deep universe agaisnt Things Man Was Not Meant To Know(tm)<br /> <br /> That's really not a point of contention in mage's cosmology. The notion of a vaccuum of space and &quot;void&quot; only appearing during the ether debacle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T16:10:00-07:00","id":1447477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1446626-anyone-else-dissapointed-with-article-4?p=1447467#post1447467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again, that's assuming that this vaccuum existed back then.<br /> <br /> Howether, it's pretty contradicted by victorian mage's futures fate.<br /> In one of them, the ether is adopted by the order of reason, which run contrary to the notion of a vacuum.<br /> <br /> I would also add that skyriggers *did* pass the horizon, as they already fought in the deep universe agaisnt Things Man Was Not Meant To Know(tm)<br /> <br /> That's really not a point of contention in mage's cosmology. The notion of a vaccuum of space and &quot;void&quot; only appearing during the ether debacle.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, a brief referral to real world facts: it was well known that there's nothing to breathe in space long before the theory of ether was first proposed. I forget exactly when it was established; I think it was in the 17th century. The theory of Lumineferous Ether wasn't about whether or not you can breathe in space; it was about how light waves move through the vacuum of space. Waves imply a medium; and Lumineferous Ether was the hypothetical medium that was being implied. No one ever proposed the idea that the Ether was something you can breathe. So unless peoples' understanding of science in Mage lagged a century or two behind the real world, the \u201cwhole Ether debacle\u201d has nothing to do with whether or not you can breathe in Conventional Space. <br /> <br /> Second: I never said that the skyriggers didn't pass the Horizon. I said that at the time, the Horizon was at the edge of Earth's atmosphere. So they never had to pass through the vacuum of space to get into the Umbra: they went straight from Earth's atmosphere into the Umbra. <br /> <br /> And third: I found the sections in the Victorian Mage draft concerning the Ether to be poorly thought out; I can go into detail as to why, if you'd like, though I'll have to ask that you wait a bit, as I'm currently at work. I'll grant that they'll nonetheless <i>probably</i> see print; but until the final product comes out, I'm still holding out hope that my objections to them will be addressed, and at this point I'm not accepting them as established fact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T18:06:34-07:00","id":1447502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1446626-anyone-else-dissapointed-with-article-4?p=1447477#post1447477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, a brief referral to real world facts: it was well known that there's nothing to breathe in space long before the theory of ether was first proposed. I forget exactly when it was established; I think it was in the 17th century. The theory of Lumineferous Ether wasn't about whether or not you can breathe in space; it was about how light waves move through the vacuum of space. Waves imply a medium; and Lumineferous Ether was the hypothetical medium that was being implied. No one ever proposed the idea that the Ether was something you can breathe. So unless peoples' understanding of science in Mage lagged a century or two behind the real world, the \u201cwhole Ether debacle\u201d has nothing to do with whether or not you can breathe in Conventional Space. <br /> <br /> Second: I never said that the skyriggers didn't pass the Horizon. I said that at the time, the Horizon was at the edge of Earth's atmosphere. So they never had to pass through the vacuum of space to get into the Umbra: they went straight from Earth's atmosphere into the Umbra. <br /> <br /> And third: I found the sections in the Victorian Mage draft concerning the Ether to be poorly thought out; I can go into detail as to why, if you'd like, though I'll have to ask that you wait a bit, as I'm currently at work. I'll grant that they'll nonetheless <i>probably</i> see print; but until the final product comes out, I'm still holding out hope that my objections to them will be addressed, and at this point I'm not accepting them as established fact.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, etherites breathes in space. And ethership are pretty much open spaces. So it's obvious in game that ether as space is breathable in ether enlightened science","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T18:26:23-07:00","id":1447505,"title":"","content":"This is covered in the Void Engineers Convention Book: on Earth, you have three Umbrae alongside the physical world; when you cross the Biospheric Horizon, physical space continues on as Conventional Space while the three Umbrae that exist within it merge into what the Void Engineers call Subspace and what the Etherites call Etherspace. This situation continues all the way out to the Spatial Horizon; and when you cross that, you end up in the Deep Universe, where there's no Conventional Space, but no Etherspace either. <br /> <br /> Etherites breathe in <i>Etherspace</i>. They do not breathe in Conventional Space, and never have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T04:20:26-07:00","id":1447559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1446626-anyone-else-dissapointed-with-article-4?p=1447505#post1447505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is covered in the Void Engineers Convention Book: on Earth, you have three Umbrae alongside the physical world; when you cross the Biospheric Horizon, physical space continues on as Conventional Space while the three Umbrae that exist within it merge into what the Void Engineers call Subspace and what the Etherites call Etherspace. This situation continues all the way out to the Spatial Horizon; and when you cross that, you end up in the Deep Universe, where there's no Conventional Space, but no Etherspace either. <br /> <br /> Etherites breathe in <i>Etherspace</i>. They do not breathe in Conventional Space, and never have.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because there was no conventional space before the rejection of the ether","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T05:41:16-07:00","id":1447564,"title":"","content":"This is perhaps not the best area of Mage to have a discussion of Earthly Foundations. There's a lot of room for interpretation when it comes to the nature and history of space. It's already more malleable than the rest of the world and most of the research and exploration we have on it comes through Mages and is colored by their paradigms. Etherspace and the current conventional space could easily rest on the same foundations and just arise from different interpretations of those same points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}